   "limitations": "Not compared frame by frame with an emulator. The hash-gated private library exports all 832 native body/cannon variants: 1,072 sequences, 4,670 frames and every one of the 67 real SPOSE rows for the Power, Full and Suitless families where they exist. Its semantic map resolves 662 gameplay bindings with no missing binding; the 18 suitless speedboost, skid, screw attack and shinespark combinations are explicitly unavailable because those abilities cannot coexist with the suitless campaign state. All palette rows and their native effects are exported and selected by SamusUpdatePalette. SamusUpdateGraphicsOam selects the per-ACD tables and falls back to the exact pose row; SPOSE_SAVING_LOADING_GAME with lastWallTouchedMidAir selects the three native InShip tables. The native C11 importer writes the library; C unit tests audit the decompilation's pose enum against the generated pointer tables and the body/cannon selection rules, and recorded digests guard every library file, palettes included; gameplay captures cover suited and suitless movement, weapons, palette effects and the Ruins Test reflection.",
