   "limitations": "The H-blank WIN0H writes are a per-line table read by the PPU (line y takes the value computed for line y - 1, line 0 its own), and the register keeps the last line's value once the H-blank stops. The runtime has no soft reset, so gDisableSoftReset's lock has nothing to lock. The ending text is English only. The Time Attack record is kept in the runtime's unlock file (version 2) rather than its own SRAM block. GM_CREDITS follows (mzm.cutscenes.credits). Not compared with an emulator. The escape ship's EFFECT_CUTSCENE_ESCAPING_CHOZODIA freezes the room, fades it out and enters the sequence on the non-gameplay screen from the ROM bank; --chozodia-escape starts it directly. After a 16-step fade in it plays the five native stages with their lengths (312, 224, 304, 280 frames, then the letters up to 472): the mother ship door opening and the blue ship growing out of it and diving (double-sized affine objects, matrix 0), then climbing away; the mother ship heating up (sChozodiaEscapeShipHeatingUpPal / GroundHeatingUpPal rows, ever faster shaking), its white explosion growing as an ellipse (sHaze_PowerBomb_WindowValuesPointers stretched by 1.2, window 0 with brightness up inside); the crater with the decaying mother ship, its explosions and the flash fading by alpha then to black; Zebes with the ship far away, then flying past the camera with the escape music; Samus in her ship turning grey (ApplyMonochromeToPalette of sChozodiaEscapeMissionAccomplishedPal) with the English MISSION ACCOMPLISHED letters revealed one every four frames, and the fade out. Its five sounds, the music fade and the escape music play. Before the sequence, the current slot receives the English completion bit for its difficulty and a separate versioned, checksummed options file receives the ending gallery bit and difficulty clear; first-clear and first-hard transient flags feed the later pop-ups. A bank-backed test checks the fades, stage lengths, sounds, explosion window, grey palette and letters; captures of every stage and one from the escape ship in chozodia_092 show the sequence. It is entered through ColorFadingProcess_ChozodiaEscape: the screen cut to black at once, then the ending save (unit-tested, captured in chozodia_092). The Time Attack is ported (mzm_time_attack.c): TimeAttackCheckSaveFileValidity (the first four bosses in order, each past sTimeAttackAntiCheatTimes), CheckUnlockTimeAttack's unlock value (the sums of the boss timers' fields shuffled with the region, sanity checks on the tanks and abilities), and for a Time Attack run TimeAttackCheckSetNewRecord: the Any% and 100% records with their 20-character password from TimeAttackGenerateSeed (88 seed bits; the native 62-byte array is written past its end and read back), its eight shuffles and TimeAttackRandomizeSeed, ENDING_FLAG_FIRST_TIME_ATTACK_CLEAR (the empty 0xFF record) and ENDING_FLAG_NEW_TIME_ATTACK_RECORD. The port was compiled against the decompilation's own time_attack.c with stub globals: identical results on 200 000 random cases (24 185 unlocks, 150 201 records); three of those vectors are a unit test.",
