   "limitations": "The soft-reset lock and the Gallery, Sound Test and Time Attack Records Options entries are not ported (the records are saved but cannot be viewed yet). The bundled NES game is deliberately outside the project scope. The ability count reads the obtained items, unknown ones included, as gEquipment.suitMisc and beamBombs hold them. Ending and pop-up text is English only. Not compared with an emulator. After the Chozodia escape, ChozodiaEscapeGetItemCountAndEndingNumber computes the ending from the maximums (sTankIncreaseAmount of the difficulty), the abilities, the difficulty and the in-game hours, and GM_CREDITS plays from the ROM bank with the credits music: the US sCredits lines scroll at 7/16 pixel a frame over the dark Chozo wall, each built from sCreditsCharactersGfx (white, blue and red rows, the two-row white names, the copyright lines) and written by the V-blank into BG0, or BG1 half a tile aside for an odd width; at the end line the wall fades in and the text out, the wall scrolls down to its bottom (513 frames), zooms into the Chozo drawing and fades to black (961 frames). The end screen then slides and blends Samus's poses (sEndingSamusPosingGfx_1 to _5), the last by ending (full suit for image 0, helmet off for 1, suitless otherwise, through the white palettes), with the drifting space background, and fades out. EndingImageInit then selects one of the eight native ending illustrations, loads the English text and the exact clear-time and collection-rate digits into OBJ VRAM, slides both background halves into place and reveals CLEAR TIME, the timer, YOUR RATE FOR COLLECTING ITEMS IS, the percentage and NEXT MISSION letter by letter on their native schedule. At 22.93 seconds it waits for A, B or START, fades the music over 256 frames and ends at frame 1664. A bank-backed test checks the ending numbers, the first credit line, stage lengths, final pose, image number, 03:04:05 and 100% graphics, letter promotion, permanent lines, input gate, music fade and exact ending frame. UnlockedOptionsInit then opens the native window over its blue panel; the English Gallery, Sound Test or Time Attack Records message is drawn eight characters per frame, A closes the panel at frame 128, and a first clear shows only Gallery. The new-record OAM badge is also supported. The first-clear, difficulty-clear and gallery-image state persists in a separate versioned, checksummed global options file, while the current slot persists its difficulty completion bit. The tests check the first-clear panel, its window geometry and rendered pixels, the other message priorities and the unlock file's checksum. A Time Attack run now produces ENDING_FLAG_FIRST_TIME_ATTACK_CLEAR and ENDING_FLAG_NEW_TIME_ATTACK_RECORD (mzm.cutscenes.chozodia_escape).",
