   "limitations": "US version (the cutscene opens with a fade to black; the upgrade's stage 19 returns IGC_RESULT_NEXT_STAGE and stage 20 keeps running). COLOR_FADING_GETTING_FULLY_POWERED's white fade is stood in by the COLOR_FADING_CANCEL fade to black. At the cutscene's end the status screen's fully powered items sequence runs (mzm.menus.status_screen); without the ROM bank every obtained item is activated at once instead. The upgrade's BG0 alpha fade (stages 2 and 18) is kept as state but the room's BG0 keeps its own blend when drawn; the flash is an additive rectangle, stretched to the view's edges when window 1 reaches the GBA screen's, and the HUD is drawn above it. The upgrade is cleared on a room change. Not compared with an emulator. The Ruins Test's despawn requests the cutscene: the room freezes and fades out; at the fade's end (ColorFadingProcess_GettingFullyPowered) the fight stage becomes STARTING_CUTSCENE, EVENT_STATUE_VARIA_SUIT_GRABBED is set (with EVENT_VARIA_SUIT_OBTAINED and EVENT_SKIPPED_VARIA_SUIT when the Varia Suit was skipped) and the Varia Suit is obtained. The cutscene runs from the ROM bank on the non-gameplay screen: Samus on BG2 and the backdrop on BG3 (pages 0x1E and 0x1C, 512-pixel-high maps), sGettingFullyPoweredSuitPal in both palettes, the ring and sparkles in OBJ VRAM; Samus brightened (BLDY to 12 by the sprite effect) outside window 1, which ends half a block below the ring; the ring rises at a pixel a frame with its palette cycled through OBJ row 10 every third frame, six sparkles spawn around it after random delays (sRandomNumberTable) and five rise from below the screen (delays read from the background graphics' bytes, as natively, including the first timer landing on the ring); BG2 and BG3 scroll down to Samus, window 1 is switched off, the whole screen brightens to white while the ring flies away faster, then the end after a second (MUSIC_GETTING_FULLY_POWERED_SUIT_CUTSCENE). The status screen then shows the items being enabled (mzm.menus.status_screen); back in the room (RoomLoad's PAUSE_SCREEN_FULLY_POWERED_SUIT_ITEMS return) the Gravity Suit is held back, Samus facing the foreground at (24.5, 31) blocks with pause disabled and the charge reset; the closing reflection shows the banner, whose removal starts the suit upgrade (InGameCutsceneUpgradingSuit, waiting for no power bomb): BG0 faded out and hidden, window 1 opened two pixels wide on Samus, grown vertically by 4 then horizontally by 7 pixels a frame with BG0's tile 0xC0 (palette 9) blended at 13/16 over the screen inside it and SOUND_ACQUIRING_GRAVITY, the Gravity Suit activated at stage 11 (Samus's graphics follow), the window shrunk back (InGameCutsceneCalculateSuitFlashOffset), BG0 restored, then RUINS_TEST_FIGHT_STAGE_SUIT_ANIM_ENDED, lastWallTouchedMidAir and gDisablePause cleared. Checked in chozodia_042 with the `--ruins-test-end` staging (the actor sent straight to RUINS_TEST_POSE_CHECK_GHOST_DISAPPEARING): the cutscene at frame 700 shows the ring, its sparkles and the brightened Samus; the return shows the fully powered suit and the banner at 392,496; after B the window grows from x 120-122, the purple flash (tileset 56's tile is solid colour 0x7C19) covers the screen at stage 13, the Gravity Suit is active (items 0x60) and the fight stage reaches 8, after which the pillar falls. The same in-game cutscene module plays IGC_GETTING_VARIA after the Varia Suit's status screen (brinstar_027: the window at x 118-120 growing, then shrinking at stage 14, the suit active).",
