   "limitations": "Not compared with an emulator; the fight was seen by capture but not won in game. Not ported: the Ridley spawn cutscene effect and the statue opening one of its death, the minimap chunk update, and the wings' frozen palette offset read from their OAM frames (offset 0). The claw's hold keeps SamusSetPose(SPOSE_HURT_REQUEST) when it drains Samus's last energy (the native follows it with SPOSE_MIDAIR); SSC_RIDLEY_CLAW's hurt adds the runtime's knockback velocity. Ridley needs EVENT_GRAVITY_SUIT_OBTAINED (and is gone with its ground blocks once EVENT_RIDLEY_KILLED is set); it locks the room and waits in the ceiling until Samus stands on the ground facing left near the platform's left or the door, then drops, breaks the ground blocks, spits ascending fireballs for five seconds (turning toward Samus), and takes off. Idle, it floats (sRidleyIdleYOffsets), slides along the ground toward Samus and turns at walls; it attacks with small fireballs on the ground, big fireballs in a fan, and its tail (gSubSpriteData2 with the eight tail sprites: diagonal and vertical swipes that shake the ground); 200 damage taken or its death forces the big fireballs then the tail. Its claw grabs Samus from above (SSC_RIDLEY_CLAW: RidleyCheckGrabbing), carries and lifts her in front of its mouth, drains her energy by the difficulty and Varia Suit, spits fireballs at her (SSC_HURTS_SAMUS_STOP_DIES_WHEN_HIT_NO_KNOCKBACK) until a timer or her mashing frees her, a wall dropping her. Its palette rows change at a half and a quarter of its health, the camera locks on Samus near the ground or held, and its death flickers it in explosions and PE_MAIN_BOSS_DEATH, fades the music, then sets EVENT_RIDLEY_KILLED, unlocks the doors, plays the boss killed music and explodes the tail. Checked by capture in ridley_012 (the drop, the fireballs, the grab lifting Samus and draining her, her release) and by a test (the Gravity Suit condition, the parts, the trigger, the landing, the 200 damage threshold and the death's event).",
