   "limitations": "SpriteCheckOnScreen uses the GBA screen size while the runtime view is wider. Room sprite placements, sprite graphics, the sprite RNG, animation and collision core, sprite families (a family whose OAM tables are missing is reported and disabled alone), secondary sprites (SpriteSpawnSecondary), whole and per-part rotation, the Zoomer crawl, turns and falls, Samus contact damage with knockback and screw attack kills (one hurting contact per frame), beam and missile hits (missiles tumbling off the sprites they cannot hurt), stuns with the stun palette flash (SpriteUtilUpdateStunTimer), freezing (SpriteUtilUpdateFreezeTimer in every ported AI, the frozen and stun rows baked as /frozen and /stun library variants), frozen and SSC_SOLID / SSC_SOLID_CHECK_COLLIDING sprites as solid platforms (SpriteUtilSamusStandingOnSprite: Samus stands on them, is pushed below them or stopped at their sides), SSC_ZIPLINE grabs (SPOSE_ON_ZIPLINE under the zipline from mid-air or spinning, SPOSE_MORPH_BALL_ON_ZIPLINE inside it from morph ball mid-air or ballsparking, gPreviousXPosition moved with her), frozen sprites dropping Samus from a zipline (SPOSE_MID_AIR_REQUEST), SP_SOLID_FOR_PROJECTILES sprites (every projectile only sets their solid hit, with its own impact particle; the Plasma Beam goes through), and death with its explosion particle into enemy drops are ported. Sprites draw by drawOrder (1 in front), orders 9 and above behind Samus (SpriteDrawAll_LowPriority before SamusDraw) and the others in front of her; SSC_CAN_STAND_ON_TOP sprites only let Samus stand on them; SP_ALWAYS_ACTIVE sprites keep running while gPreventMovementTimer stops the others; secondary sprites draw with their spawning sprite's graphics. During any screen shake, Zoomers and Zeelas on the screen stop crawling and those on walls or ceilings fall (SpriteUtilShouldFall). SSC_HURTS_SAMUS_A_LOT hurts with five times the stats damage and a knockback a subpixel stronger; the contact damage follows the difficulty (halved on easy, doubled on hard, after the suits) and the sprites see gSamusWeaponInfo.chargeCounter, last frame's gArmCannonY / gArmCannonX and gDifficulty. A capture in brinstar_000 and brinstar_001 shows the yellow and red Zoomers crawling along floors, walls and ceilings (one climbs a wall from y 406 to 451 in 90 frames).",
