   "limitations": "gLastDoorUsed is not tracked: the landing happens in the room a new game starts in (the runtime's `landing` flag), never when entering the room through a door. The palette animations (GunshipEntranceFlashingAnim's OBJ row 9 and GunshipFlickerFlames' row 10) are baked as library variants of every combination, the runtime drawing the gunship's sprites with the rows last copied. The mosaic status is not drawn. The escape (Mother Brain killed), EFFECT_CUTSCENE_EXITING_ZEBES and the complete Tourian escape handoff are connected, but the take-off is untested in a full playthrough. The new file's COLOR_FADING_LANDING_SHIP fade in is not drawn. Not compared with an emulator. \"A new game from the file select starts in Crateria's first room with the gunship six blocks up landing in 3.2 seconds (SOUND_GUNSHIP_LANDING, the vertical then horizontal flames, the HUD hidden, the pause disabled), Samus inside it (SPOSE_SAVING_LOADING_GAME with lastWallTouchedMidAir, drawn with the native in-ship animation behind the ship); half a second before touching down it starts the intro text, which leads to the game's start in Brinstar. On the ground the gunship's entrance opens and its platform rises while Samus is near; Samus standing on top (SSC_CAN_STAND_ON_TOP) enters it (turning from the foreground, sinking with the platform behind the closing entrance), is refilled (energy, missiles, super missiles, power bombs with the HUD's refill animations and SOUND_GUNSHIP_REFILL), gets \"\"Weapons and energy fully restored\"\", then the save prompt: yes saves the file (the gunship's saving sound and \"\"Save complete\"\"); then she rises out of the hatch and faces the screen. A file saved there resumes with Samus rising out of the ship. Checked by capture: the landing and its fade into the intro text, entering, the refill, the save and leaving in crateria_000. The tests run the landing, entering, the refill, the save prompt and leaving.\"",
