   "limitations": "The location texts are baked in the banner's graphics by the exporter (English only), as /ltN library variants; the banner always draws as graphics slot 7 (its slot of the spriteset only matters for the palette rows, which are baked). gLastDoorUsed is known for door transitions and the new game's start (door 0); a loaded file shows only the save and map room banners of their spritesets. The banner is drawn after the front backgrounds (BG priority 0) at its GBA screen position, the GBA screen centred in the wider view. Not compared with an emulator. SpriteUtilInitLocationText: when a room is entered through a door flagged DOOR_TYPE_DISPLAYS_ROOM_LOCATION (exported as Y lines) the area's location text (LocationTextGet*: BRINSTAR, KRAID, NORFAIR, RIDLEY, TOURIAN, CRATERIA, CHOZODIA, MOTHERSHIP, PLANET ZEBES, CHOZO RUINS, the map rooms...), and in a save or map room spriteset always its name, put an area banner in sprite slot 0 at an absolute screen position: an area's name scrolls in at the bottom for 2 seconds (sAreaBannerLocationTextPal), a room's name in the middle for 1.5 seconds (5/6 of a second for the save and map rooms, none of those while the alarm rings), then scrolls out. TextDrawLocation's text (mask mode over 0xFF, its two tile rows copied to the graphics slot) is drawn by the exporter with the native font. Checked by capture: BRINSTAR at a new game's start and SAVE ROOM in brinstar_033. The tests run both banners and the alarm case.",
