   "limitations": "The corrupted file handling and the supported options (stereo, sound test, gallery, time attack records and Fusion link) are not ported: the options entry is shown but A on it does nothing. The bundled NES game is deliberately outside the project scope. The Japanese text menu is skipped as in the US version. A new game plays the gunship's landing in Crateria (mzm.environment.gunship) and the intro text cutscene (mzm.cutscenes.story_text), then starts in the runtime's first room. FileSelectCopyFileHandler is ported from its NON_MATCHING C version. The text buffers' fills follow the US binary, which adds their offsets in bytes where the decompiled source's u32 pointers would scale them (checked in the disassembly of mzm_us.elf). Not compared with an emulator. \"START on the title enters the US file select screen on the native screen PPU: the Chozo background, the menu and panel tilemaps from the ROM bank, the three files with their energy and tanks (HudDrawEnergy into the file's tiles), timer or dashes, difficulty and area, the Metroid logos of completed files, the music, and the fade in. UP and DOWN move between the files and the enabled entries (with the maintained input repeat) with the file markers and Samus's head cursor; B fades out to the intro (GM_INTRO). A on a file opens its \"\"Start game\"\" panel (the window, the alpha fade and the BG2 scroll), whose text is drawn line by line with the native font; A there continues a saved file (the start animation, then the save is loaded), or on a completed file offers continue / new game / time attack and the overwrite confirmation, and on a new file opens the difficulty panel (hard once unlocked, completed difficulties highlighted) before the start; B closes the panels back. Checked by capture: the files, the panels, a new game and a continued file. Copy (with at least one file) chooses a source among the used files (a time attack file is refused with its message) and a destination among the other files (the first empty one, else A/B), shown by the green markers and the arrow, confirms the overwrite of a used destination, copies the file (SramCopyFile) and redraws it; erase chooses a used file, confirms it (NO by default) and deletes it (SramDeleteFile) before redrawing; B leaves each step. The runtime copies and deletes the save files themselves. The Time Attack code is ported (FileSelectCheckInputtingTimeAttackCode: UP, LEFT, RIGHT, DOWN one key at a time in a completed file's Start game panel once gFileScreenOptionsUnlocked.timeAttack bit 0 is set, a wrong key restarting it after half a second): it opens Continue / New / New Time Attack on New Time Attack, and a new Time Attack game keeps SaveFile.timeAttack (save version 4) for gTimeAttackFlag. A bank-backed test enters the code.\"",
