   "limitations": "The item acquisition, suitless and fully powered suit sequences are ported; the debug status screen is not. StatusScreenToggleItem only toggles during the suitless and item acquisition sequences, as natively. gCurrentItemBeingAcquired is tracked by the runtime from the item and tank banners and cleared when a file is loaded. UpdateSuitType has only its suitless and fully powered cases. The demo stages of StatusScreenSuitlessItems and TextProcessDescription are never used (no demo runs). The English text pointers are always used. Not compared with an emulator. \"R on the map screen runs PauseScreenStatusScreenInit: the R prompt and its visor overlay, the opening sound, the map fades out through BLDALPHA (PauseScreenInitFading / PauseScreenApplyFading, two levels a frame), the status BG2 with its blend, the headers and Samus's wireframe (sSamusWireframeData, sSamusWireframePal by suit, an OBJ window copy showing only BG3 and the objects) slide in, fade in, become their linked versions, the equipment rows are revealed one a frame (StatusScreenDrawItems) and the cursor and text BG0 appear. PauseScreenInit draws the status tilemap from the runtime equipment (obtained and activated items, the plasma beam, gravity suit and space jump as unknown items before the fully powered suit, the bombs and missiles with their ammunition, the pistol when suitless) and the energy and ammunition amounts. The D-pad moves the item cursor between the enabled slots (StatusScreenGetDestinationSlot with the remembered left and right slots), each slot writes its description with the native font into the text tiles (TextProcessCurrentMessage, TextDrawCharacter with the ROM character widths and graphics), A skips the delay and turns the lines, and B, L or R goes back to the map (PauseScreenQuitStatusScreen). Checked by capture in brinstar_000 (long and charge beams, missiles, bombs, misc items). The fully powered suit's items open the status screen on its own (BG2, OBJ and the OBJ window; BG2 blended at 22/16 on BG2, BG3, OBJ and the backdrop) after UpdateSuitType(SUIT_FULLY_POWERED) refills Samus and deactivates every item: Plasma Beam, Gravity Suit and Space Jump stay unknown rows and the missile rows inactive; PauseScreenSuitChangingStart shows the upgrade headers, reveals the rows and puts the cursor on gCurrentItemBeingAcquired's slot; the suitless wireframe fades to the full suit (PauseScreenFadeWireframeSamus) after 50 frames; the normal items are enabled one by one with the cursor's destroy animation and SOUND_ENABLING_NORMAL_ITEM; each unknown item gets its overlay object (MISC_OAM_ID_*_UNKNOWN on OBJ row 12), two partial and one full white flash, SOUND_ENABLING_UNKNOWN_ITEM, its name row written, the cursor, SOUND_TOGGLING_ITEM_ON, the known overlay, the flash fading back, then its description with the names' idle palette until A (the Gravity Suit activates and fades the wireframe to its palette); every item is then activated and the screen leaves after 12 frames. A unit test runs it on the ROM bank; captures in chozodia_042 (`--ruins-test-end` with test items) show the Plasma Beam and the Space Jump unknown, then revealed and described (\"\"Somersault continually\"\"). The item acquisition (PAUSE_SCREEN_ITEM_ACQUISITION, after a new item's or first tank's banner) and suitless (PAUSE_SCREEN_SUITLESS_ITEMS, after the post-Tourian monologue, with UpdateSuitType(SUIT_SUITLESS)) sequences open the status screen on its own: StatusScreenGetSlotForNewItem deactivates the new item, PauseScreenSuitChangingStart puts the cursor on it, StatusScreenSuitlessItems toggles it back on after 16 then 8 frames (SOUND_TOGGLING_ITEM_ON, SOUND_UNKNOWN_ITEM_ACQUISITION for the unknown items; a suit fades the wireframe; the item's missile or bomb row lights up), then describes it and leaves on any key. As natively, StatusScreenToggleItem's 0xFF result stored in an s32 is never below 0, so the toggle stage always runs. Unit tests run the Varia Suit, a first missile tank and the suitless sequence on the ROM bank; captures in brinstar_027 (the Varia Suit taken from its statue: the banner, the status screen with \"\"Decreases damage taken from enemies.\"\", then the in-game suit flash) and after the Tourian escape (the suitless status screen with the pistol described, then chozodia_000 with the Power Grip, Long and Charge Beams active).\"",
