   "limitations": "Liquids and the speed booster and shinespark aura sprites (gScrewSpeedAnimation) are not ported. With the Speed Booster, running above 96 subpixels a frame counts a timer to 160 (the cap rises to 140 at 120 and 160 at 140); from 160 subpixels a frame SamusCheckShinesparking starts the speed boost (sound, Running_Speedboosting, the speed boost palette rows by gFrameCounter8Bit % 6, the 160 ground and mid-air caps kept through jumps and the speed-boosted landing), cancelled below it and on death. Releasing the direction skids (10 subpixels a frame, the skidding sound); Down alone while skidding, or during the six frames after a speed-boosted roll in the Morph Ball, stores a shinespark for 180 frames (the palette and the charge sound every 16 frames). Speed boosting breaks speed blocks (DESTRUCTING_ACTION_SPEED and SPEED_ON_GROUND) and kills weak sprites as DCT_SPEEDBOOSTER with its particle and sound. Checked in tourian_010 with --item speed-booster: the speed boost palette and running animation after about 160 frames of running. With a stored shinespark, A (without a direction on the ground, with half a block of room, Samus rising by it) or A in the air starts the charge (50 frames of glow, the shinesparking sound, no gravity); when its animation ends the spark goes up by default at 192, sideways at 192 with the direction held, or diagonally (160, 96) with L or the direction and Up, through SamusSetPose with the speed boost on, killing weak sprites as DCT_SHINESPARK (its particle and sound). A ceiling or a wall ends it in the collision (48 frames of invincibility, the collision sound), 17 frames, then the delay after and a fall. In the Morph Ball with High Jump, A starts a ballspark: half a block up, a hop on the first frame, one second of charge with the ballsparking sound and the ball turning toward the input, then the same sparks, the collision and the Morph Ball fall. SamusSetPose stops the sounds when a charge or spark is cut short. Checked in tourian_010: run, skid, Down, A: the spark rises to the ceiling, then the delay after.",
