   "limitations": "Each background is rendered alone by the PPU and the runtime composes them with its sprites by priority, so the BG0 blend is approximated by SDL blending (additive at EVA/16, alpha at 16 - EVB) instead of the GBA's per-pixel targets; the block layers are redrawn around the view every frame instead of the native row and column streaming (the same tiles); the mother ship common tiles (gUseMotherShipDoors, set by door types) are not tracked; the lightning background effect, BG0 and BG3 movement (clouds, snow), the 0x43/0x44/dark-room BG0 positions, haze, gradients, windows and screen fades are not reproduced; without the ROM bank the exported metatile sheets are drawn instead (static). The camera is the runtime's 320x224 follow view. With the ROM bank, mzm_room_gfx rebuilds the room's VRAM and BG palettes as RoomLoadTileset leaves them (animated tiles at 0x4000, common tiles at 0x4800, the tileset at 0x5800, the BG3 graphics below 0xFDE0, palette rows 0-2 common and 3-15 from the tileset), decompresses the BG3 and LZ77 BG0 maps, sets the BG control registers and priorities of TransparencySetRoomEffectsTransparency, and writes the block layers' metatiles (gTilemap, then gCommonTilemap past block 1024) into the 512x256 maps around the camera. Every frame it runs AnimatedGraphicsUpdate (16 slots with their five types, mirrored at the end of VRAM for slots 12-15), the tank animation, AnimatedPaletteUpdate on palette row 15 (disabled without the alarm or the ziplines event, paused during a power bomb), the hatch flashing, and positions a liquid LZ77 BG0 from gEffectYPosition with the water wave (sWaterLoopCounterArray), which also feeds the hazard and sprite liquid surface. Lava, acid and water now animate and blend: checked by capture in norfair_022 (lava), crateria_007 (water over Samus and the Skulteras) and brinstar_000. Screen shakes (mzm_screen_shake, one shared state as gScreenShakeX/Y): a longer shake replaces the current one; once a frame a 2-pixel offset every third frame (up or left, then down or right with intensity bit 0, else nothing), halved in the last quarter second, moves BG0 to BG2 and BG3 by half, never the sprites; the room load clears them. Checked by capture during a power bomb in chozodia_005 (BG1 2 pixels left, then back). A BG_PROP_MOVING BG2 (crateria_016, kraid_030) follows ScrollBg2: BG1's position plus gBg2Movement, kept within BG2 for the GBA screen (the runtime's wider view may show past it). The shared background-effect processor now implements the quick, slight-yellow and heavy-yellow native tables: it snapshots BG rows 0 to 14, pauses during transitions and power bombs, advances one command per frame and restores the exact palette; `--background-flash` captures verify the quick sequence while ROM-free tests cover all three.",
   "next_action": "Port the lightning background effect, BG movement and haze, then compose the layers with the sprites per pixel.",
