   "limitations": "The bitmap modes 3 to 5 are not rendered, but a source audit proves the pinned MZM program never selects them. Registers are sampled by the host renderer rather than hardware dots; the Chozodia escape's only required H-blank rewrite is represented by its per-line WIN0H table. Affine reference latching, the object cycle limit and affine-object mosaic are not hardware-cycle emulated. The ROM bank contains the whole verified ROM privately and is never committed. The register bank keeps BG2/BG3 affine registers independent from the lower display registers. The renderer covers every display path selected by MZM: modes 0 to 2 text/affine backgrounds, all regular and affine object shapes, 1D/2D mapping, flips, double size, windows and object windows, alpha and brightness effects, mosaic, priority and forced blank. The intro, title, file select, pause/status, Game Over, credits, Tourian escape and Chozodia escape run through it and have tests and recorded captures. The native hash-gated private bank indexes 14,462 sized ELF objects and is generated by the C11 importer in the rebuild graph; mzm_rom resolves names and GBA addresses and implements the BIOS LZ77 and run-length streams. ProcessComplexOam and CalculateOamPart4 are shared by the affine escape scenes. The technical audit rejects any future use of unsupported bitmap modes.",
