   "limitations": "The runtime writes its own versioned little-endian files (header, payload, CRC-32; version 3 with gInGameTimerAtBosses, versions 1 and 2 still read) instead of the GBA SRAM layout with its copies and checksums; a file keeps the room alias, Samus's position and facing, the equipment, the events, the minimap progress, the collected items, the opened hatches, the never-reform blocks, the area, the difficulty, the in-game timer, the timers at the four bosses and the completed game flags, but not the music or the rest of gSamusData. gMostRecentSaveFile is the newest of the three files. The save completes in one frame instead of the multi-frame SramSaveFile stages. The difficulty is kept and applied: the contact damage (halved on easy, doubled on hard), the tank increases, the stun threshold (CONVERT_SECONDS(.24f) on hard) and the bosses' difficulty branches. Three files, file_a.sav to file_c.sav in --save-dir (else SDL's preference folder). YES on a save platform's prompt writes the current file through a temporary file renamed over it. The file select screen reads their info (SramWrite_FileInfo: existence, area, energy, missiles, suit, timer, completed flags, difficulty) and continues one: its room is loaded and its state restored with Samus in SPOSE_SAVING_LOADING_GAME and gIsLoadingFile set for the room's first sprite update, so the save platform releases her; --load does the same at start with the most recent file. The in-game timer runs each game frame as InGameTimerUpdate does (frames, seconds, minutes, hours, capped at 99:59:59 with gMaxInGameTimerFlag). Truncated, corrupted, foreign or newer files are rejected. The file select screen's copy and erase menus copy a save file over another or delete it. The game over's continue loads the most recent file the same way, or restarts the game's start without one. Version 3 adds gInGameTimerAtBosses (Kraid, Mother Brain, the Ruins Test and Mecha Ridley record the in-game timer at their death, as natively). Checked in game through the save platform of brinstar_033 (the prompt, the save, then the reloaded file).",
