   "limitations": "Not compared with an emulator. (An earlier note claimed the charged trail had a native low BG priority: ParticleChargedPistolTrail never sets PARTICLE_STATUS_LOW_BG_PRIORITY, so its bgPriority is 0, as the runtime draws it.) Suitless Samus automatically charges the pistol every frame: B fires the harmless normal shot before 112 frames or the charged shot from 112 through the 127-to-112 wrap, with the native two/six projectile limits, seven-frame cooldown and shot sounds. Both shots use CAA_BOMB_PISTOL, travel 22 subpixels per moving frame without the short-beam lifetime and use their native directional OAM and hitboxes; the charged shot drops PE_CHARGED_PISTOL_TRAIL every eight frames. The normal shot always produces an invincible hit. The charged shot deals 12 to sprites weak to charge shots or beams, but a Space Pirate is instead paralysed for 60 ticks with the suitless black/purple flicker and no damage. The projectile exporter stages the pistol graphics and palette for its muzzle flash and charged trail. Checked in chozodia_000 after the Tourian escape and the suitless status screen: facing left, a tap of B fires the uncharged shot; 130 frames later (the counter charges by itself, without B held) a second tap fires the charged shot, whose PE_CHARGED_PISTOL_TRAIL particles follow it left at 66 pixels per 12 frames while the counter restarts from 0. The capture diagnostics now list the charge counter and the projectiles.",
