   "limitations": "MP2KPlayerMain is ported for its sequencer clock and channel gates only: FadeOutBody and track LFOs are incomplete. CGB channels are allocated but neither computed with MidiKeyToCgbFreq nor synthesized; SoundMainRAM reverb and XCMD pseudo echo are not ported. The mixer runs at the host fixed 60 Hz step rather than the GBA 59.73 Hz VBlank and has not been compared by ear or against an emulator. TrkVolPitSet runs without modCalculated LFO state. Track-address ordering is represented by player and track indices. PORT, XCMD and the native tempo-to-VBlank scheduler are absent. Room music derives save, warp and transition flags from any room map cell rather than the cell under the camera; unk_37E, boss-mode and unk_4BE event branches stay clear, and the transition fade flag is not cleared because that path is not traced. aos_mp2k_engine_load_bank now shares engine_replace with init and set_bank, restoring the 0xFF host player gains a compound-literal reload used to zero; regression tests cover init/set_bank/load_bank defaults, per-player muting and failed-load preservation, and the browser --check renders both title pulses to nonzero PCM. The native C11 importer reads all 495 gSongTable entries plus each fixed MP2K header, and aria_sound exports their header pointer, player, channel, track count, block count, priority and reverb into a private manifest guarded by a golden digest. The Aria runtime loads the player and priority fields before PlaySong runs and advances MPlayVolumeUpdate once per lifecycle frame. A bounded host-neutral MP2K track decoder now reproduces the native wait clock table, running status, FINE, GOTO, three-level PATT and PEND, REPT, EOT, note parsing and the PRIO, TEMPO, KEYSH, VOICE, VOL, PAN, BEND, BENDR, LFOS, LFODL, MOD, MODT and TUNE state changes. Invalid pointers, recursive command loops and unsupported PORT or XCMD streams fail closed. Source-derived and unit-tested, not emulator-compared. The private MP2K bank (0x0827B2C0-0x084F08F8: the voice groups the song headers use, from the decompilation's audio segment, through gMPlayTable and the song data) is exported as sound/runtime/sound_bank.bin; aos_mp2k_player_start reads a song header (track count, block count, priority, reverb, voice group) and starts each track at its pointer, failing closed outside the bank. StartSong calls it only after its player-priority replacement accepts the song. A local --check run initialized all 495 song headers of the exported table. aos_mp2k_player_frame ports MP2KPlayerMain's tempo clock: each frame the counter (+ 0x22) gains the interval (+ 0x20); while it is at least 150 every existing track advances one clock, MP2K_event_tempo sets the raw tempo to twice its value and the interval to raw * scale >> 8, the clock (+ 0x0C) counts, and a clock that finds no track ends the player (+ 0x04 = 0x80000000); then the counter loses 150. The runtime runs it for every player each frame after the volume update. A local --check ran all 495 songs for 600 frames each: 340 ended and none hit an unsupported or invalid stream. The channel side of MP2K_event_nxx is ported: each note (logged with the voice and track priority current when it was read) resolves its tone from the voice group (key split 0x40 through its key table, rhythm 0x80 with the entry's key and pan, a nested split or rhythm dropped), takes priority min(255, player + track) and a channel: its CGB channel when free, stopping, lower or equal from a track not before it; otherwise the first free of the 8 DirectSound channels of DEFAULT_SOUND_MODE, else the best stopping one, else the lowest active one not above it. Gates count down at each track clock and stop their channel at 0; MP2K_event_endtie stops the newest unstopped channel of the track with its key; MPlayStart's TrackStop stops and unlinks the player's channels. A local --check gave 5640 channel notes and 54 dropped ones over 600 frames of every song. TrkVolPitSet (volume split by pan, key shift and pitch from bend, range, tune and the public controls), ChnVolSetAsm (each channel's right and left volume from its velocity and rhythm pan) and MidiKeyToFreq (gScaleTable as its closed form, gFreqTable, the 178 clamp) are ported; they run at each note and after every player frame for the linked channels, which gives the values the native VOLSET and PITSET flags guard. A local --check read every DirectSound sample's rate from the exported bank (none outside it). SoundMainRAM without reverb is ported as aos_mp2k_mix: per frame each DirectSound channel's envelope steps (a start begins the attack with the wave's loop flag, attack to 0xFF, decay to sustain, release on a stop down to the echo volume, the echo countdown), its mix volume is (right + left) * envelope >> 9 with master volume 15, and 176 signed 8-bit mono samples at 10512 Hz (DEFAULT_SOUND_MODE, divFreq 798) are mixed with the native wrapping byte sums: fixed-frequency tones one sample per output, the others linearly interpolated in 23-bit steps of frequency * divFreq, looping waves restarting inside their loop. The runtime plays it through an SDL audio stream (--mute disables it) and can record it (--audio-wav); --play-song requests a song at the start. A local offscreen run recorded 600 frames of song 1 as 105600 samples, 95 percent non-zero, RMS 10-15 per second. sub_08013960 is ported as aos_room_music_enter and runs at the start and at each room change: save and warp rooms quiet the music, transition rooms mute player 0 once (sub_08013F6C(0x1040)) and forget the song, other rooms set it loud and play the area's song (sUnk_084F106C, sUnk_084F1086 for Julius) or a room's special song (0x2A, 0x27, 0x29, 0x25 by their room and event bits), stopping the previous one. The sound export writes metadata room_music.tsv (save and warp bits of the map table 0x08116650, transition rooms from sUnk_0850E968: 17 save, 8 warp and 16 transition rooms). A local run of room 0/3 recorded the area's song with no --play-song. The held-sound list unk_254C4 of sub_08013D60 / sub_08013E18 (4 slots scanned from the last) is ported as aos_audio_hold and aos_audio_release. When the portable sequencer reaches FINE or fails, aria_runtime clears the mirrored PlaySong player-active state; a finished higher-priority effect can no longer reject later lower-priority Soma sounds on the same player. This lifecycle is deterministic and unit-tested. m4aMPlayVolumeControl now propagates each volume ramp into every MP2K track's volPublic field. The host also mirrors MPlayStop and m4aMPlayContinue into the portable sequencer: a stopped player releases and detaches its live channels, does not advance, and resumes at its saved stream position. This prevents replaced opening-scene music from continuing underneath its successor. Patch 0778 adds a host-only per-player mixer gain after native channel volume calculation; the shared launcher cross-fades player 0 while player-5 SFX remain audible, without mutating MP2K state. The focused mixer test covers isolated player output. The START pause hub, the SELECT quick map and their closes now issue SONG_QUIET (0x1012, ramp to 0x90) and SONG_LOUD (0x1011) instead of the pause/resume pair: sub_080473F4's mode entry issues no stop command, so gameplay music keeps playing at reduced volume like the native menus.",
   "next_action": "Listen to and compare the output (emulator capture), then port the CGB channels (MidiKeyToCgbFreq, CgbSound), the reverb path, the LFO, and wire the native PlaySong requests of rooms, monsters and menus.",
