   "limitations": "The palette-fade processor that applies sub_0803D18C / sub_0803CDF0 each frame is not decompiled: fades are modelled as their traced step (sub_0803E8BC) added once per frame until the target. The runtime shows the BG and OBJ fades with a colour modulation and a black veil, and the frontend the game-over fades with a veil (exact for one shared weight). The 0x42C & 0x200000 restart branch of sub_0800C8C8, the death fade now plays SONG_MUTE at sub_0800C8C8 case 0 and GameModeGameOverUpdate requests MUS_15 at stage 0 and SONG_MUTE at the stage-3 press through the lifecycle song drain. sub_0801B03C is decoded: a drifting sparkle entity (callback sub_08045C9C = our drift flag) runs on Soma himself (called from his state-16 update with player +0x1E = 4): each axis acceleration opposes its velocity sign at 0x200 (+-0x200 terminal oscillation, a slow drift rather than a halt — ported in death_state) and, while flag +0x58 bit 0x20 is clear, emits an animation-0xD effect every four frames (+0xD counter & 3) at his position plus two sub_0802D5EC(0x80000) rolls with y offset -0x100000. The runtime now emits AOS_EFFECT_SPARKLE drift effects on the same four-frame cadence and 8x8/-16px box during soma.state 16; the corpse sparkle now uses AOS_EFFECT_DEATH_SPARKLE (Effect/death_sparkle, sequence 13 of 0x0820ED60 with palette bank 4 — sub_08045CEC(x, y, 0xD, 8) where arg3 nibble 8 selects the OBJ palette row, not the descriptor bank which the 7-bank palette 0x082099FC caps at 6). The runtime hands over to the frontend process (--frontend, --game-over) rather than switching mode in one process, and no save is touched (the native game over returns to the Konami logo). Death art verified: anim 0x33 maps to Soma/animation_051 (5 frames) in the exported runtime index, sound 0x197 plays on die(), state 16 keeps drifting in the +-0x200 oscillation and the runtime spawns the documented sparkle every four frames; the corpse sparkle plays the native animation-13 sequence (Effect/death_sparkle). The post-game-over path (GAME_OVER -> KONAMI_LOGO -> TITLE -> file select) matches the native mode chain, so continuing reloads a save through the frontend file select. sub_0800C8C8 case 1 decodes a second branch: when unk_42C & 0x200000 is set the death reloads instead of game-over (unk_A074_1 = 0, unk_42C gets 0x800000, room transition sub_08011F44(0x085236A4) then sub_08011AD0, brightness decrease, GAME_MODE_IN_GAME); the flag is never set in the decompiled sources or the six non-matching functions, so the branch is documented but unported (dead code or set through a block write). Soma's death (sub_0801AF20) enters the in-game death sub-state: sub_0800C8C8 fades BG to black over 0x40 frames and OBJ over 0x80 and enters GAME_OVER once the OBJ fade has ended. GameModeGameOverUpdate shows BG1 in 256 colours (tiles 0x080E5C08 and 0x080E5C10, palette 0x080E6A3C, map 0x080E9584; the background renderer now supports 8-bpp tiles), fades it in from black over 0x20 frames, waits 0x80 frames, creates the language's GAME OVER sprite at (0x80, 0xE) and blends it in over 0x20 frames (BLDALPHA from EVA 0 / EVB 16 to 16 / 0), waits for any new press, fades to white over 0x20 frames and returns to the Konami logo. The runtime runs the death fade (Soma died at frame 284 in room 0/3 and the game over followed at frame 412) and relaunches the frontend with --game-over, which shows the native painting and sprite from the ROM and continues through the boot modes. An offscreen render of the screen showed the native painting with 'Game Over'. Source-derived and unit-tested, not emulator-compared.",
