   "limitations": "\"The page now renders 0x36A \"\"Pause the game?\"\", 0x34B \"\"Yes\"\", 0x34D \"\"No\"\" (native leading space) and the 0x361 cannot-save message through the native cell engine: shared sub_08040748(0,0,26,3) window, question at cursor home, Yes at sub_0804066C(4,1), No at sub_0804066C(0xC,1), all context A — matching sub_0804BD38/sub_0804BE0C. The message-window frame and the selection arrow remain OBJ-layer work, and nothing is emulator-compared.\" Sleep defaults to No, accepts Left or Right selection, refuses B or No, snapshots the current room, Soma, progression, equipment, inventories, souls, MP and button assignments, then writes a companion quicksave. Success requests song 0x1010 and runs the source-timed 64-frame darkening plus 33-frame reset tail. The frontend exposes the companion at the native odd position; loading consumes it once and keeps the regular file as the persistence target. Copy and delete remove the destination companion. Source-derived and unit-tested, not emulator-compared. The render keeps the native string IDs, small font and bottom text band; the Yes/No cursor cells (4,1)/(0xC,1) map to pixel columns 24/72. CORRECTED layer model: gDisplayRegisters points at BG0CNT (hw 0x04000008), so sub_0805AE64 writes BG0CNT=0x1C04 (map block 28 = 0x0600E000 strips map, 256x256, priority 0, palette 1, char base 1 = 0x06004000) and BG1CNT=0x1D01 (map block 29 = 0x0600E800, char base 0 = 0x06000000 window sheet); bgOfs[0]=0. sub_0803FD9C(desc,dest,mode) DMAs desc[3]<<9 bytes to dest directly: window sheet -> 0x06000000, language bank -> 0x0600A000, engine glyph sheet -> 0x06004000 (unk_11598, 32 tiles/row 4bpp grid). BG0 char base 1 reaches tiles 0x000-0x3FF covering 0x06004000-0x0600BFFF: strips (tile 0x060+), engine-rendered frame tiles AND language-bank glyphs (bank at tile offset 0x300). The whole dialogue box is effectively BG0 + BG1 sheet layer, clipped by WIN0 x[40,240]/WIN1 x[0,40] y[120,152].",
   "next_action": "Port the BG0/BG1 composition: strips + engine frame tiles + bank glyphs on the 0x06004000 char space, BG1 sheet layer on 0x0600E800, WIN0/WIN1 masks, then remove the SDL backing panel.",
