   "limitations": "sub_080683BC is ported for its experience reward and drop decision. Its two remaining gates are boss-rush flags that only GameModeBossRushMenuUpdate sets (unk_60.unk_4CC_0 = bits 0-1 of +0x4CC skipping every reward, and unk_60.unk_A1_4 = the high nibble of +0xA1 raising the unowned-soul chance 6 to 7 and scaling the damage calc by 8/10); boss rush is not ported, so both stay clear as natively in normal play. The level-up display sub_080455BC is ported (aos_levelup: still frame 0x48 on OBJ row 6, the sub_08045454 sine spin/scale envelope, the unk_A074_0 entity-update freeze, sub_08045270 sparkles and PlaySong(0xBC)); the Sherman Ring walking-experience path of sub_0801B0D8 (_0801CCE2) is ported: accessory 0x2A, LEFT or RIGHT held, ticks&7==0 before +0x22 advances, AIRBORNE and WALL clear, unk_42C bit 0 and 0xA074 bit 1 clear grant one point into +0x1328C capped at 0x05F5E0FF, then the level loop and sub_080455BC(0). Enemy rewards are connected only for reconstructed enemy entities. Bestiary and common/rare discovery words use a ROM-free portable representation rather than native SRAM. sub_08033DA4 starting stats for Soma and Julius, sub_08033DFC's x(x + 1)(3x + 8) thresholds, sub_08033CAC's level loop to 99 with its four gain tables, sub_08033E10, sub_08033E38 and sub_08033E6C are ported. The experience part of sub_080683BC grants each enemy record's reward once, marks its bestiary bit, applies the bonus flag and cap, and levels up; its drop part preserves the native soul, item and fallback-pickup decision order. The runtime creates and collects the resulting soul, item, money or MP-heart entities, records common and rare discovery bits, and schema-v9 saves preserve all three discovery sets. Source-derived and unit-tested, not emulator-compared.",
