   "limitations": "The hub uses the source BG1, portrait, frame, language-bank labels, digit tiles, palettes and BG0 layout decoded directly from a verified ROM, plus the selected entry's info line (text 0x362+entry via sub_0804728C rendered through the native cell engine aos_menu_cells with ROM metric/glyph tables; window geometry still estimated pending the fb-to-tilemap decode); its cursor OAM and exact fades remain absent. Soul Set uses its source BG0 labels and coordinates, stats, palette selection, ROM-localized equipped/list names and descriptions, and both native proportional fonts. Equip uses source list ordering and a native BG0 data view with ROM-localized equipment text and stat comparison. Both subpages still lack their title/frame and icon/cursor OAM layers; Soul Set's list order is verified as an index-order scan of the +0x38 count array in sub_0804B494 (soul ids 0..0x1F filtered by nonzero count, scroll top at +0x15, selected at +0x16); soul ownership is the 0x13260 bitfield plus per-soul absorb counts; souls DO have the same recent-four mechanic as equipment: sub_08049E64 caches the four most recently collected souls per colour family at +0x133DC/+0x133E0/+0x133E4 on every soul pickup and sub_080494F8 lists those owned entries before the index-order remainder (ported through AosRecentSouls); exact category transitions remain unverified, and L/R remains a source-adapted colour shortcut. Config draws its native label and button-name strips, Sleep its native Yes/No strings, and Ability its sub_0804BA18 window fill, twelve row strips, per-ability ON/OFF tile pairs and localized names (0x156-0x15B or 0x34F) on BG0; all still lack their OBJ cursor, window frame and icon layers. Item Use draws its native BG0 grid, names, quantities and empty-slot dashes (icons stay OBJ); Enemy's list and detail views draw their native BG0 layouts while both lack the portrait, OBJ icons, soul message window, header/footer decorations and exact transitions. Pause and native menu sounds are requested through the native audio controller, but the MP2K host is not emulator-compared. Cursor OAM located: the selection hand is a dedicated sprite entity at gEwramData+0xE2C - sub_08048AD8(cell_x,cell_y) writes its position as x*8+6/y*8+3 and sub_08048B0C frames it through sub_0803B924 with OAM tables 0x08256EF8 (shared with the portrait frames) or 0x0827B1F0; its tiles come from the menu OBJ upload, not the object library. Frame path decoded: sub_08048B0C picks table 0x0827B1F0 instead of 0x08256EF8 when *(gEwramData+0x4D0)==3, passes selector entity+0x11 and palette nibble 0xE to sub_0803B924, which caches the resolved frame at ctx+0x64, merges the palette into ctx+0x5A bits 3-6 and commits OAM through sub_08000FBC; sub_08039614 resolves (table,selector) by walking the runtime animation lists at gEwramData+0xFEC8 (stride 0x14 records) headed by +0x11072/+0x11074, then indexes 16-byte frame descriptors at +0x10178; sub_0803E654(2) seeds ctx+0x2C and ctx+0x65 takes the caller's frame argument. Ported for the hub: aos_pause_graphics decodes the hand sheet and frame descriptor per language (0x082052D8/0x0827798C/0x0826C840 graphics with 0x08256EF8/0x0827B1F0 frames, the same pairs sub_08048C74/sub_08048B0C select) plus the 0x0820C2C0 palette blocks and draws record 6, the extended pointing pose, at sub_08048AD8's cell (1, selected+0xC); the The cursor now animates: records 2-8 cycle at four ticks a step and sub_08048018's horizontal +-3px wiggle is reproduced from the shared frame counter. Soul set's second sub_08048EA4 call site uses the identical formula and the enemy detail view has no native hand placement, so all cursor placements are covered. Cursor placements ported on all seven pages: hub cell (1, selected+0xC), sleep (1,0x10), ability ((cursor&1)?0x10:2, 4+2*(cursor>>1)), item use ((slot&1)?0x10:1, 0xB+slot/2) on the owned ordinal minus scroll top, equip (2, 5+2*slot) on equipped rows plus the item list's flat slot formula, config (5, cursor*2+4), soul set ((slot&1)?0x10:2, 0xA+slot/2) on the selected-minus-top soul slot, enemy ((slot&1)?0x10:2, 5+slot/2) on the ten-entry page; soul set's second sub_08048EA4 call site uses the identical formula and the enemy detail view has no native hand placement, so all cursor placements are covered. START freezes gameplay and opens the seven-entry hub through the source-derived sub_08047520/sub_08047C4C presentation in native order: Soul Set, Equip, Item Use, Ability, Sleep, Config and Enemy. Repeated Up/Down wraps the cursor; A enters all seven usable pages; B returns from a page and B or START from the hub resumes play. The Soul Set renderer reconstructs sub_08048D84, sub_080493E8, sub_080494F8 and sub_08049DB4, while the Equip renderer reconstructs sub_0804A95C, sub_08049F34, sub_0804A2A4, sub_0804A00C and sub_0804A120 from the verified ROM without tracked extracted assets. Soul Set equips owned coloured souls, Equip changes all three equipment slots and previews all six affected values, Item Use consumes owned usable items, Ability toggles owned ability souls and draws their native BG0 page and Config applies unique action-button assignments. Sleep creates a one-use quicksave from the current runtime state and returns through the frontend after its source-timed fade. Enemy lists the source's 112 visible records, gates details on defeat and shows exported combat, drop and soul facts. The schema-v9 save bridge persists inventories, selections, button mappings, bestiary and drop discoveries at the next save-room write. Source-derived, deterministic-tested and verified-ROM image-checked; not emulator-compared. The hub info line prints text 0x362+selected.",
