   "limitations": "Souls are collected, counted and equippable through the source-adapted soul page. Many red attacks and every blue and yellow effect remain unported; ability toggles are stored, while their movement effects still use the diagnostic move mask. The soul pickup is drawn with the soul0-3 sequences of the shared 0x081C15F4 resource (palette cycle of sub_08032B14), and its trail spark is now emitted as a type-8 sub_08045B44 child (position offsets of sub_0802D5EC(0x200000), velocity -soul/4, acceleration soul/64, soul-kind palette via the container-spark kinds; its animation plays the type-4 {3,7,7,3} ticks rather than the native type-8 {2,4,4,2} entry and its own RNG draws are not made), the held-soul sparkle sub_08045BC8/sub_08045164 is ported as the pinned AOS_EFFECT_SOUL_HELD effect (Effect/soul_held sequence 12, palette bank 6, offset (0,-0x100000) from the player's +0x44, song 0xBF after 0xBC for a repeated soul; a new soul's sparkle natively waits for the unported icon's 64th frame so ours spawns immediately) and the new-soul entity sub_08045C34/sub_08045654 is ported as a 48-frame spawn state (combat->soul_storm) emitting sub_08045350's type-0x49 sparkle (update sub_080451F4: 21-frame life, drift velocity offset>>4 with -(offset*5)>>4 decel, frames {0x49,0x36,0x35,0x34} cycled one per 8 frames via table 0x08525138, soul-kind palette) spawned at the player plus sine/cosine * 48 for 48 frames as AOS_EFFECT_SOUL_STORM0-3 direct effects (frames {0x49,0x36,0x35} at 8/8/5 — the 21-frame cap ends before the fourth table frame), then the same held sparkle; sub_0800E708 now shows the obtained-soul banner on every accepted soul collection, with sub_0800E540's description only when the soul is new (sub_080441F8's GetSoulTotal == 0 branch sets arg2 = 1) (name text = 0-based index + 0xE3/0x11B/0x133/0x156 per kind, description = 0x1E4/0x21C/0x234/0x257 + index through the shared AosSoulNotice composition, upper banner row when Soma's pixel y passes 0x70, 0xF0-frame lifetime standing in for both unk_422 values (0xF0 name-only, 2 description-path, units unresolved)), sound 0xBC plays on collection; sub_08049E64 is ported (the recent-soul caches feeding the Soul Set order). Soul pickups created with a non-zero last argument (state 0x63, the palette-cycle states) are not ported. The soul inventories keep native nibble counts in two groups per colour (red 2 x 28, blue 2 x 13, yellow 2 x 18 bytes) and a single ability array that both groups read, so an ability soul counts double as natively; SoulInventory_AddAmountToGroupTotal clamps a group to 0-9 and AddAmountToSoulTotal first takes the amount back from group 1 when it holds some and the total would pass 9. sub_08032ADC enables an ability bit and sub_08032DBC counts collected souls up to 999. Cases 5-8 of sub_080441F8 also call sub_08049E64, which caches each collected soul id in its colour family's four-entry recent list at +0x133DC/+0x133E0/+0x133E4 (1-based ids, duplicates skipped, a full list loses only its last entry); the runtime records the same caches through AosRecentSouls. sub_0804459C creates a dropped soul heading away from a random point above Soma (one draw) at speed 0x30000; sub_080446D4 turns it toward Soma's y - 16 (sub_0802D408 over ArcTan2, step + 0x2A per frame up to 0x4000), speeds it up by 0x1800 up to 0x80000, makes the trail's two random draws on even timer values and lets it live 200 frames plus 64 blinking. Cases 5-8 of sub_080441F8 add it, enabling an ability soul's ability when new. The runtime creates souls from enemy drop rolls (now with the equipped accessory, effective LCK and held-soul test), runs move, collision and trail in that order, and saves the souls (schema v6). Source-derived and unit-tested, not emulator-compared.",
   "next_action": "Port the remaining red attacks, blue and yellow effects, then connect ability toggles to the movement upgrades.",
