   "limitations": "The standalone SDL frontend selects the host-neutral boot path and consumes typed slot/name requests. Both startup logos are drawn from the ROM (aos_logo_graphics), but the language menu of GameModeResetUpdate (not shown by the US build) and the menu and introduction graphics remain partly diagnostic. The logos' VRAM before stage 1 is not modelled: the stage-0 frame shows the new logo under BLDY 16, which is a white screen either way. Gameplay still launches as a separate process; explicit room, save, capture and debug launches intentionally start at IN_GAME. The host-neutral handler table connects Reset, both startup logos, all currently reconstructed title stages, MAIN_MENU, INTRO_CUTSCENE and IN_GAME. The SDL title host persists regular-file menu operations, runs the introduction for new files and launches gameplay only after its native IN_GAME handoff. Source-derived and unit-tested, not emulator-compared. Both startup screens are now drawn natively: stage 1 of GameModeLicensedByNintendoUpdate (character resource 0x080E5C00 on block 0, the palette resource 0x080E6838, BG0 0x080E94F4) and of GameModeKonamiLogoUpdate (0x080E5C18, row 0 of 0x080E6C40, BG0 0x080E9614), decoded by aos_logo_graphics and rendered through BLDCNT's brightness effect: the Nintendo screen fades in from white and back to white (BLDY by 2), the Konami logo fades in from white (BLDY by 1) and out to black, as the native controllers set BLDCNT. The BLDY fade-in now ends as the original's 'if (bldY > 1) bldY -= step; else bldY = 0' does, on the frame BLDY reaches 1 or 0 (the Konami fade-in was one frame long). The preview plays SE_428 when the Konami code was entered. The decoded logos were checked by eye (rendered images); not emulator-compared.",
