   "limitations": "The title screen (GameModeTitleScreenUpdate) is ported in aos_title_screen with its stages, palette system, BG1 wave, its entities and their OAM list, and its three backgrounds and three object sheets are decoded natively (aos_title_graphics). Divergences: the menu has no SOUL TRADE entry (deliberate: no link cable on a PC); no Julius mode (deliberate): the name JULIUS entered on a completed file is an ordinary name, not sub_080083C8's code for character 1, so GAME START sits 4 pixels lower (0x8C - 4 * count) and the rows slide by the parity of their shown position; the affine objects (the swooping bat, the sparkles) are mapped as whole frames, without the per-component double-size clipping of sub_0804342C; the OBJ pixel picks the lowest priority, then the lowest OAM index, a simplification of the hardware's per-pixel OBJ selection; the swooping bat's frames were not compared with the game. The main menu's objects follow sub_080069C4 with these divergences: the SOUL TRADE screen (sub_0800656C) is not drawn; for a cursor above a file (4F9 from 6) the summary is the file's own, where the game reads SRAM slot 4F9; components with the alternate tile base (+ 9) use the normal one; the portable saves keep no completion flag (+ 0x2D), icon set (+ 0x2E) or map completion (+ 0x32), so the stars, second icons, completed file's second time and percentage show as 0; the area name's 12 glyph rows exceed the one map line sub_08046DD4 writes, so its lower rows are cut, as the code reads; the other languages' two-line area names are not ported; the cancel's palette fade to black is replaced by the host's BLDY overlay. The PLAY prompt ignores the 0x381/0x38B special-mode branches of sub_08005908. Gameplay still launches as a separate process. The decompilation's nonmatching sub_080083C8 body is source evidence but is not emitted as a separate static-inventory symbol. The lifecycle connects title stages 0-9 to all three native main-menu operation controllers. PLAY retains its file/quicksave and special-mode topology; COPY and DELETE retain their cursor and confirmation paths. Native name entry retains wrapped editing and its special codes. The verified-ROM renderer reconstructs the base, PLAY, COPY, DELETE and name-entry background planes in all three languages. aos_main_menu_prompt_id selects the localized prompt (0x354-0x356 base, 0x35B/0x35C PLAY, 0x358/0x359/0x379 COPY, 0x35A/0x377 DELETE) as sub_08004928, sub_08005908 and the copy/delete controllers do; the frontend reads it from the ROM text table (control 6 new line, 10 end) and draws it with the native proportional font. All ten prompts parse in the three languages of the verified ROM (optional local test). The SDL launcher consumes typed regular-file and quicksave requests, runs the opening controller for new files and waits for its IN_GAME handoff. Odd quicksave entries load their one-use companion and retain the regular file as the next persistence target. Source-derived, unit-tested and ROM-smoke-tested; not emulator-compared. GameModeTitleScreenUpdate runs natively: the 32-frame fade-in, the moon's affine zoom and rotation (BgAffineSet, frameCounter * 16) and wobble, the 49-frame cycle of BG row 0 through 0x080E622C with its 48-frame fades, entity 0x12's 45-frame sweep of OBJ rows 4-7 that ends stage 4, the bats' alpha of stage 6, the logo (BG1) revealed through a decaying H-blank wave, the castle (BG0), the white flash of the backgrounds and the red tint of the objects, the menu (GAME START, then the extra entry and its BOSS RUSH / SOUND TEST submenu with the slide of sub_0800432C), the START shortcut, the 600-frame idle timeout and the exit fade; the objects: entity 0x12's disc (frames 0-3 of 0x0820CB1C on rows 4-7) eclipsing the moon, then (stage 5) the OBJ window that hides BG2 inside it (WINOUT 0x3F / 0x3B); the 34 bats of sub_08003DBC from the seed 0x1967 (sub_08003A9C's ten random values each, their drift toward (0x78, 0x60) and wobble), shown at the end of stage 5 and semi-transparent until the end of stage 6; the swooping bat of sub_08003CF8 spiralling in to (0x7A, 0x1A); the two rotating sparkles of sub_08003F08 at 0x40000, sparkle 0 driving BLDALPHA, deleted after 87 frames; sub_08000EA8(1) deleting them at the reveal; the menu sprites of sub_0800427C and entity 0x15's ring and copyright (sub_080044DC). Object priorities come from their layers through sub_0803DD14's thresholds (6, 7, 0x16), and sub_0803FD60 gives BG1 priority 0, BG0 1 and BG2 2, which puts the logo in front of the castle. The SDL preview renders it all through a GBA-style compositor (priorities, OBJ window, semi-transparent objects, alpha and brightness effects) and plays MUS_27 and SONG_MUTE through the exported song table and the native MP2K mixer (--mute disables it). The final menu frame was compared by eye with a screenshot of the game (screenshots/aria of sorrow title screen.png): same layout and colours except the absent SOUL TRADE. The main menu is drawn natively: aos_main_menu_objects loads entity 0's three sheets per language (0x082052D8 icons and cursor, 0x082052E0 font, 0x080E5BC0 labels with the frame descriptors 0x082571E0, 0x08259120, 0x08267A38) and the OBJ palette of sub_0803C74C(0x080E5E24); aos_main_menu_sprites builds sub_080069C4's OAM list with sUnk_080E0CC0's six styles (the labels lit on row 5, the ornament's animation 0, the hand's 3-pixel wobble and blinking, the file icons, NEW GAME and quicksave marks, the names glyph by glyph, the name-entry grid and caret); aos_main_menu_files writes sub_08006D9C's level, map per mille, play time and gold as 0xD100 digits, maps the area name's text line (context B, row 6 + panel, text 0x3B7 + area) and gives BG1's H-blank offset of sub_08007204 (0x88 on 0x50 lines for an empty PLAY file) and sub_0800737C (0x88 on 0x40 lines for a used COPY target). The controller now queues the menu's PlaySong calls: MUS_14 at stage 0, SE_239-SE_244 where sub_08004928, sub_080074C0, sub_08007914, sub_08007B8C, sub_080083C8 and stages 6 and 9 play them, the name codes' 0x1E5, 0x1B5 and 0x199, SONG_MUTE on cancel and STOP_SONG + MUS_14 (sub_080049C4) on leaving; the cancel waits for its 0x20-frame palette fade (sub_0803D06C) instead of a host flag. The SDL preview reads the gamepad, takes scripted presses (--press) and screenshots (--screenshot); its screens were checked on such screenshots with portable saves, not compared with the game.",
