   "limitations": "Gameplay starts as a separate process, and the introduction has no emulator pixel comparison. The seven-stage controller retains all native durations, scrolls, blends, skip destinations and the sub_08008ED0 handoff. Its six-actor group preserves fixed-point motion, thresholds, lifetimes, alpha ownership and cleanup. sub_080093E0 retains the complete row-oriented script protocol. The verified-ROM resource view resolves the three language banks, proportional font, complete background palette, two compressed character banks, three block maps, both actor sheets, all ten supporting frame records, both supporting animation streams and all four OBJ palette rows without exporting proprietary bytes. The controller steps Soma's four 42-frame stair poses and the affine actors' six three-frame poses. The SDL host renders BG3 through BG1 at their native fixed-point scroll positions, maps white text through palette row 15 and composes all six actors with their resource record, native OBJ row, layer-derived priority, inverse affine scale and panel alpha. Source-derived, unit-tested and ROM-smoke-tested; not emulator-compared. The frontend now delivers the native MUS 21 start, sound 318 affine-rise cue and 0x1010 exit mute to MP2K. sub_08008FEC's second panel draw is rendered 128 pixels from its first, following the source's integer high-halfword offset. A fidelity pass against GameModeIntroCutsceneUpdate corrected the BLDALPHA packing: alpha_pack now stores EVA in bits 0-4 and EVB in bits 8-12, matching C_16_2_8, so the panel blend (EVA 6/EVB 10), the stage-4 pulse and the stage-5 flicker carry the native coefficients. The SDL host now feeds semi-transparent OBJ pixels from the merged alpha_blend register instead of the per-frame entity override, and stage 6 renders the sub_0803D18C/sub_0803CDF0 palette fade as a brightness ramp to black over 0x78 frames. The stage-5 flicker uses the native RandomNumberGenerator recurrence seeded with sub_08004160's 0x1967 new-game value. A presentation pass removed the leftover A/START skip debug overlay (the native skip path is unchanged) and stopped wrapping the three decoded bitmaps during the stair scroll: the native offsets stay within height-160, so each layer is drawn once and the castle no longer superimposes before its native arrival.",
