   "limitations": "fusion_metroidvania runs both native title screens at once, separated by the source prototype's patch-0046 animated geometry: eight staggered Metroid bipolar triangles and eight staggered Aria Fermat spirals rotate clockwise at 10 degrees a second, without the later polarity mirror. X uses Zero Mission SOUND_RUINS_TEST_SHOOTING_LIGHTNING 0x1DC and Y uses Aria sound-table entry 0x081. Independent host-only per-player gains cross-fade native music player 0 while leaving SFX players audible at every divider angle; neither sequencer state nor native volume is changed. Holding either key for three seconds selects its existing runtime once through fusion_host, while releasing early cancels. The supplied JSON values are compiled defaults and --split-config accepts an optional strict JSON override. START retains the title-driven in-process launch flow. Limitations: startup sequences, idle introduction and demos remain deliberately skipped; the Aria menu-to-gameplay chain inside the launcher was not run in this cycle. Deterministic tests cover native-ID routing, separate player gains, geometry, JSON, hold and cancellation; headless captures cover composition. Sound choice is source-derived and locally waveform-reviewed, not emulator-compared. aos_mp2k_engine_load_bank now restores the 0xFF host player gains like init and set_bank (a shared engine_replace), so bank-loaded engines no longer mute every MP2K player; fusion_aos_mp2k_tests covers the defaults, per-player muting and a failed load, and fusion_sfx_browser --check now renders the Aria 0x081 and Zero Mission 0x1DC pulses offline and fails on silent PCM. Held X/Y pulses now climb one semitone per 0.5 s beat from six below the native pitch (saturating at +12) through host-only per-player pitch controls (aos_mp2k_player_pitch key_shift_public, mzm_audio_set_player_pitch in the native pitch routine); releasing the key resets the progression. Aria type-8 fixed-frequency channels are retimed by a host-only 16.16 playback step since they ignore channel frequency.",
