   "limitations": "A new file continues from the scrolling introduction into area 0 room 0, where Object20 parameter 3 starts ROM text entry 0x000C and holds Soma on native animation 0x51 at the lower floor position. Native portraits and distinct speaker/dialogue fonts remain connected. The portable actor model consumes all seven beats and exported animation durations. State 3 constructs and renders the six sub_0805D2C8 and four sub_0805D35C children around its 3.5-pixel-per-frame pan and two 0x20-frame holds. Type 8 uses Winged Skeleton art plus sub_0805E2D8's RNG phase and quarter-amplitude sine bob; type 10 uses Skeleton Knight art plus sub_0805E5D4's variant-gated start, optional second gate, sixteen one-in-three half-pixel rises and parameter-selected state-2 animation. Its optional parameter-bit-3 path now applies animation 1 and 160 one-in-two collision clocks, descending two pixels in air or retaining its quarter-pixel facing drift plus any wall correction when snapped to a floor. RNG, sine, ArcTan2, floor depth and wall push are injected so the same model serves runtime and editor previews; none of the current ten emission records sets bit 3. After Arikado animation 2 both callbacks run their source underflow blink and random-selector tails. In-margin impacts now create and render all seven source-table debris pieces with native gravity. Every type-10 finish creates the common-animation-0x16 projectile, which curves from 3 to 8 pixels per frame toward the principal Winged Skeleton, uses the native lifetime and target box, and plays 0xBC on contact. The scene's principal-enemy timer, music, persistence and Winged Skeleton soul grant remain connected. The return pan now plays post-script (+0xb==8 -> camera mode 4) and the post-scene proximity conversations are ported: Mina and Arikado stay in the room, the runtime re-arms an edge trigger, runs the native 0x40px box test with Arikado priority (text 0xE) then Mina (text 0xD) through the same window machine, and repeats after Soma leaves both boxes. The initial reveal remains missing; the projectile pair spawner sub_0805DC80 is dead code (unreferenced in the ROM), so no projectile callback exists in this scene. Source-derived, unit-tested and locally reviewed, not emulator-compared. The dialogue composition now follows both sub_08067934 and screenshots/dialogue.jpeg: WIN0 spans x=8..232 and opens to y=88..160; its source BLDY=8 brightness decrease now darkens BG1-3, OBJ and the backdrop before the undimmed BG0 portrait and text, the portrait is cropped four pixels upward against the reference, the native speaker and body maps begin at (40,100) and (40,116), and Object20 suppresses the gameplay HUD. The native folded-page marker is decoded from the selected language bank at x=216, y=140; its corrected payload +0x400 slice gives one complete CE/DE image phase and one fully transparent CF/DF phase without the former two-pixel ghost. The rejected pink language-sheet strips remain decoded and unit-tested but are not rendered. Object20 state 5 now removes the principal enemy at timer 0xD0, then at 0x8F renders the ROM-localized Winged Skeleton soul notice, plays 0x197, mutes music player 0 and holds Soma on pose 0x52 with alternating visibility. The obtained-soul presentation now reconstructs sub_0800E708/sub_0800E540 through a portable BG0 map and pixel sampler: the centered red banner, 30-tile description field, generated dynamic colors, rows 14/15 palettes, six-pixel scroll and folded-page phases all come from native resources and ROM-localized text. A fresh-file local run completed the story, set event 0x20 and granted and equipped the soul. The obtained-soul window (sub_0800E708) is restored as a modal state-5 step: it opens at battle timer 0x8F with the ROM text entries 0xE3/0x1E4, mutes music player 0, blocks the script until the player dismisses it, then closes before state 6 resumes MUS_23. Dialogue portraits now decode only the native portrait resources; the gameplay-sprite fallback was removed and decode failures are reported once per id.",
