   "native_routines": [],
   "limitations": "Bone Pillar now assembles its native 22-pixel linked tower and Buer emits its linked second direct frame. Per-segment and fire collision, bounce timing, attacks, fades, sounds and rewards remain open. Buer's separate native state-4 updater now raises the inert visual once by 32 pixels and advances its 0x100 orbit phase; the emitted effect remains missing. Buer's lethal state-3 dispatch now runs the native 96/128-frame death counters with 0x6E sound requests. The linked death effect and eight fragments remain absent. Buer state 2 now preserves the GBA 0xFF wait threshold and 32..63-frame RNG window/retry timing; linked motion and effects remain open. Buer state-2 proximity now starts its native 80-frame attack/32-frame recovery cycle and requests 0x84 at the source-derived frame values. Linked projectile visuals and motion still need dedicated ports. Buer's linked fire sprite now preserves its own facing bit and the source-derived one-flip-per-window timing, with correct parent velocity direction on idle restart. Native flame attacks and linked sprite effects remain incomplete. Buer state 1 now enters state 2 on the native room-boundary probe (x, y+92), without clearing the independent timer; the terrain/linked fire probes are still missing. Buer linked-fire lifetime now matches sub_080CC3C8: state 0 follows, later states freeze position, and the defeated owner retains it until removal without contact. Buer sub_080CC514 now responds to nonlethal state-2 hits by entering the state-2 attack step 1 (substep 0), without overriding the lethal death callback. The native 192x48 idle proximity gate now checks the linked-fire facing and preserves simultaneous 0xFF RNG precedence; Buer's actual terrain probes and attack visuals are still partial. The linked fire's orientation now tracks signed Buer velocity on state-1 and state-2 idle rolling ticks, without clobbering its separate attack/recovery facing. The native probe/friction and fire projectiles remain open. Buer's no-contact rolling angular path now uses the native 0x8000 initial spin, +/-0x4000 speed floor, 0x40 friction, signed /64 angle integration and state-2 idle reversal. Collision flags, bounce impulses, native translation and rendered affine rotation are still missing. Corrected Buer's source-data mapping: original +0x18 angular speed, not provisional +0x48 X velocity, now controls linked-fire facing, state-2 idle gating and the signed angular heading restored on attack expiry. Full terrain probes, projectile output and audiovisual parity are still missing. Buer has a source-derived contact bounce for simple solid wall probes: angle integrates from original +0x18 spin and wall impact reverses/halves it. Native collision mask, slopes, X translation, attacks and rendering remain partial. Buer now includes bounded floor-slope 0x20/0x40 angular impulses from native sub_080CC20C and ROM-free sign/ orientation tests; native mask assembly, movement, fire effects and linked damage remain unimplemented. State-one Buer now translates X from its native signed angular velocity before damping and abandons the artificial patrol-boundary reversal; solid-front and room-boundary rollback remain bounded approximations, not a complete native collision port. Buer state-two idle mode-six now advances subpixel X from pre-contact spin on confirmed flat ground, with no-ground and bounded wall/room rollback. Active attack motion and terrain geometry are still provisional. Buer mode-six idle now preserves Y without ground and snaps shallow flat-floor penetrations rather than using sine bob; the complete native vertical physics remains open. Buer attack angular acceleration, paired non-damaging fire visuals, and 96/128-frame death affine rotation plus flame cadence are source-derived partial ports; true projectile damage and eight native fragments remain pending. Patch 0665 replaces Buer visual fire stand-ins with independently animated paired entities and source-derived coordinates/8.0 motion, and adds death stage-two X translation. Projectile damage and ROM death fragments remain incomplete. Patch 0666 reconstructs Buer's speed-cap-triggered attack exit and recovery affine/slope angular response; original multi-point collision, fire asset frames and final eight fragments remain open. Patch 0667 connects Buer's eight native final flame offsets through local C object export and runtime metadata to one-frame death emission, with an eight-effect report and safe fallback. Terrain, OAM and projectile hitboxes remain partial. Patch 0668 reproduces Buer death-stage linked-fire wobble and native source-sized random flame regions around the linked child/old owner positions. Real affine OAM and mode-six terrain remain partial. Patch 0669 replaces fixed Buer wall/floor probe geometry with ROM-local signed multi-point probes, preserving legacy metadata fallback; native contact masks, affine graphics and projectiles remain partial. Patch 0670 fixes Buer complete 16x16 BG1 solid-block wall/floor contact and backward-compatible grounded correction; native curved masks and attack physics remain partial. Patch 0671 extends Aria Buer slope contacts to both imported floor-width edges with a centre-first legacy-safe response; collision masks remain partial. Patch 0672 gives Aria Buer mode-six idle centre/edge flat-ground gating and 8px/16px shallow correction; exact collision masks and gravity remain partial. Patch 0673 enables full source-mode Buer native walk and gravity with imported probes and SDL affine body rotation while retaining old export fallback; ROM/emulator parity is unverified. Patch 0674 matches Buer linked flame noncombat callback and paired attack animation resource failure, without guessed hitboxes or fake static sprites. Patch 0675 aligns inactive Buer rotation with the native +0x14 affine word and keeps parent versus linked-fire mirror state independent. Patch 0676 adds original zero-horizontal-speed gravity and ground contact to every Buer first-death-stage tick with available native probes. Patch 0677 emits the linked flame for inert Buer and preserves spin/gravity initialization even when the native global flag skips ordinary combat setup. Patch 0678 corrects Buer native attack-side rotation and keeps the fire sprite mirror bit synchronized with its original side byte. Patch 0679 fixes unconditional Buer gravity setup for active and inert instances without enabling unverified terrain probes. Patch 0680 matches Buer branch-specific linked-fire facing during attack spin reversal, with zero/sign-crossing regression coverage. Patch 0681 corrects the eight final Buer flame positions to GBA 4-pixel Y origin with synthetic offset and subpixel tests. Patch 0682 removes synthetic initial X speed from native Buer while retaining bounded legacy-metadata compatibility; tested before and after the first motion tick. Patch 0683 restores GBA u16 Y-plus-24 wrap in paired non-damaging Buer attack visuals; native OAM, sprite art and emulator comparison remain open. Patch 0684 corrects Buer's source attack-side spin and paired fire mirrors; counter-spinning and tied integer-X tests still keep visuals noncombat. Sprite art and emulator checks remain open. Patch 0685 corrects GBA Buer death-stage flame scatter widths to 16x16 and 32x32 instead of legacy oversized ranges. Both scatter boundaries and RNG counts are covered without ROM data. Affine visuals, graphics and live emulator validation remain open. Patch 0686 exercises Buer's complete ROM-free spawn-to-death linked-visual lifecycle and rejects missing animation resources safely. The feature remains partial pending in-game graphics, audio and soul validation. Patch 0687 adds ROM-free Buer signed-Y halfword wrap coverage for constructor and inert rotation. Native audiovisual and emulator comparison remain partial. Patch 0688 fixes GBA modulo-32-bit death flame scatter placement at signed coordinate limits without inventing art or damage.",
