   "limitations": "The SDL host runs the native boot, title, main-menu and scrolling-introduction controllers, maps typed file operations onto three checksummed portable files and one-use quicksave companions, and launches the room runtime only after the native gameplay handoff. It forwards --rom so a new file continues into the first-room Object20 opening story; schema v14 preserves bestiary, drop discovery, event words, one-time placed items, guaranteed boss souls, the explored quick-map cells and the secret-room discovery bits across later saves. With --rom the frontend verifies the user's Aria image and renders the native menu and introduction resources directly from memory without exporting ROM bytes. The main menu draws its native objects and file statistics, and the title screen is native. The scrolling introduction draws its backgrounds, white text and all six actors from the native resources, including Soma's complete stair animation, the two affine actors and the alpha panels. The panels use their source 128-pixel paired draw, and MUS 21, sound 318 and the exit mute reach MP2K. Completed-file metadata and map state remain incomplete; portable quicksaves use companion files instead of native SRAM. A fresh local file completed the first-room story and persisted event 0x20 with the Winged Skeleton soul. In gameplay, START now draws the source pause hub from its verified-ROM BG1, portrait, language tiles and palettes, while SELECT reconstructs the procedural native castle map, its four-frame BLDY open/close fades and the current-screen highlight with the explored cells persisted in save schema v13; the secret-room edges now follow the native discovery bits (marked on map visit rather than room entry), the button-config page draws its native label and button-name tile strips, the sleep page draws its native confirm strings, and the remaining START sub-pages stay diagnostic.",
